From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Take the display as on while MCE hasn't said
 otherwise

The device monitors put the modem into its screen-off mode while the
display is off: the indication filter drops signal strength and full
network state, and the modem is told low data is expected. The display
state comes from MCE, and a display state that never became valid was
taken as off. Without MCE, as on LuneOS, that is for good.

The q25's MediaTek RIL honours this and stops measuring: every signal
strength report, solicited or not, IRadio 1.4 or 1.6, came with all its
values unavailable, and oFono showed Strength 0 while registered on LTE.
Telling the RIL the display was on brought the values back (Strength 23
to 26 right away).

Take a display state that isn't valid as on. With MCE that only covers
the moment before MCE answers.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/binder_devmon_ds.c | 8 +++++++-
 src/binder_devmon_if.c | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/binder_devmon_ds.c b/src/binder_devmon_ds.c
index 9e4461c..348b9d8 100644
--- a/src/binder_devmon_ds.c
+++ b/src/binder_devmon_ds.c
@@ -122,8 +122,14 @@ static inline gboolean binder_devmon_ds_battery_ok(MceBattery* battery)
 static inline gboolean binder_devmon_ds_charging(MceCharger* charger)
     { return charger->valid && charger->state == MCE_CHARGER_ON; }
 
+/*
+ * Without MCE (LuneOS has none) the display state never becomes valid.
+ * Taking that as "off" kept the modem in its screen-off mode for good,
+ * and a RIL that honours it stops measuring the signal. Until MCE says
+ * otherwise, the display is on.
+ */
 static inline gboolean binder_devmon_ds_display_on(MceDisplay* display)
-    { return display->valid && display->state != MCE_DISPLAY_STATE_OFF; }
+    { return !display->valid || display->state != MCE_DISPLAY_STATE_OFF; }
 
 static
 void
diff --git a/src/binder_devmon_if.c b/src/binder_devmon_if.c
index dbc07ff..97526c0 100644
--- a/src/binder_devmon_if.c
+++ b/src/binder_devmon_if.c
@@ -133,8 +133,14 @@ static inline gboolean binder_devmon_if_battery_ok(MceBattery* battery)
 static inline gboolean binder_devmon_if_charging(MceCharger* charger)
     { return charger->valid && charger->state == MCE_CHARGER_ON; }
 
+/*
+ * Without MCE (LuneOS has none) the display state never becomes valid.
+ * Taking that as "off" kept the modem in its screen-off mode for good,
+ * and a RIL that honours it stops measuring the signal. Until MCE says
+ * otherwise, the display is on.
+ */
 static gboolean binder_devmon_if_display_on(MceDisplay* display)
-    { return display->valid && display->state != MCE_DISPLAY_STATE_OFF; }
+    { return !display->valid || display->state != MCE_DISPLAY_STATE_OFF; }
 
 static
 void
